-- N3 example sentences, batch 3: degree, report, and the spoken shortcuts.
--
-- 〜だけでなく, 〜ほど, 〜くらい and 〜とおり measure and compare; 〜まま
-- freezes a state. Then three things that only really live in speech —
-- 〜っけ for what you have half-forgotten, 〜って as the casual quote, 〜なんか
-- / 〜なんて for dismissal — and two that only live in formal register:
-- 〜ように言う and 〜させていただく.
--
-- Three rewordings:
--
--   予想どおり shreds to 予想|ど|お|り. とおり written in kana after a noun
--   has no entry; 予想のとおり keeps the の and cuts clean.
--
--   寝てしまった lost ま|っ|た, the same しまう gap batch 3 of N4 hit —
--   しまいました survives whole, so the sentence is polite past.
--
--   発表させていただきます came apart as 発表 | さ | せ | て. A する-verb
--   causative is two suffixes past what the index holds; 読ませて cuts clean,
--   so the humble example is about reading rather than presenting.
--
-- Additive, idempotent, safe on a live database.

  -- dake-de-naku
